 "title": "The Hague, 14 June 1778: what Dumas's operations consist of",
 "caption": "The cipher runs of Dumas's letter N2 to the Committee for Foreign Affairs, 14 June 1778 (Papers of the Continental Congress, item 93 vol. 1, image 160), with the words he wrote in clear between them. Not in the editions checked.",
 "unit": "numbers",
 "key_note": "Dumas's own key, applied unchanged (targets/dumas1777/key/key_positions.json): each number is the place of a character in 13 printed lines of his 1775 preface to Vattel, accents dropped, so every e of the passage has its own number. The words are divided as in the reading; the numbers run on. Marked doubtful: 54, which the key gives as n; the reading takes it for s (\"sont pour nous\"), a conjecture. The capital R is written in the run where the two other copies of the letter have 12 = s (\"vos amis\").",
